# Git Policy (hard constraints)

Applies to **GitHub and GitLab** (PR = GitHub Pull Request, MR = GitLab
Merge Request).

1. NEVER push to `main` / `master`, and never run `git push --force` under
   any circumstance.
2. NEVER merge a Pull Request or Merge Request automatically.
3. NEVER delete a branch, tag, remote, or remote repository without
   explicit human approval in this exact session.
4. ALWAYS create a feature/fix branch before making changes:
   `feature/<short-name>` or `fix/<short-name>`.
5. ALWAYS commit with a Conventional Commit message.
6. ALWAYS open a PR (GitHub) and/or MR (GitLab) instead of merging
   directly, then STOP.
7. Before running any of: `git push`, `git merge`, `git branch -d`,
   `git reset --hard`, `git rebase`, `gh repo create`, `glab repo create`,
   or deleting remotes — ask the human for explicit "yes" first, and show
   exactly which command will run.
8. When creating a new remote project, ask which platform(s) to use
   (GitHub, GitLab, or both) if not already specified in `AGENTS.md` or
   the human's prompt. Follow `prompts/remote-setup-template.md`.
9. Never commit API tokens, PATs, or passwords. Prefer `gh auth login` /
   `glab auth login` over embedding credentials.
10. If unsure whether an action is destructive, treat it as destructive and
    ask first.
